<title>SPAIN: Spain has nearly 100% chance to be in EMU -banker.</title>
<headline>Spain has nearly 100% chance to be in EMU -banker.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The probability Spain will be in European Monetary and Economic Union (EMU) from the start is now close to 100 percent, according to a Spanish banker.</p>
<p>&quot;The probability Spain will be in the first wave of countries taking part in Europe's single currency is now close to 100 percent,&quot; said Pedro Luis Uriarte, managing director of Banco Bilbao Vizcaya (BBV) at a seminar.</p>
<p>&quot;It's even higher than the probability of some core countries,&quot; Uriarte said.</p>
<p>He added that both the government and the Bank of Spain were &quot;working hard&quot; toward such an achievement.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
